<author><name>Google</name></author>
<category scheme="urn:rss-system-design:subject" term="genai-apps" label="LLM Apps &amp; Agents"/>
<category scheme="urn:rss-system-design:subject" term="ml-platform" label="ML Platform &amp; Models"/>
<category scheme="urn:rss-system-design:concern" term="cost" label="Cost Efficiency"/>
<category scheme="urn:rss-system-design:concern" term="evaluation" label="Testing &amp; Evaluation"/>
<category scheme="urn:rss-system-design:concern" term="scalability" label="Scale &amp; Performance"/>
<summary>Shows the design decision to route coding-agent tasks with a cheap classifier from Flash-Lite to Gemini 3.8 Flash on low thinking, and its trade-off with per-model context caching, after a keyword heuristic fell to 70.6% on held-out tasks.</summary>
</entry>
